      {
        "id": 91763,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-17T18:28:37.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"lynkfox\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/48/1997_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lynkfox:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We need to get a better Search function to prevent these duplicate posts <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> (<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/quick-mdp-environment-question-4723\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/quick-mdp-environment-question-…</a> )&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>We need to get a better Search function, yes…but I doubt anything will prevent rank newbies from showing up and never once considering that anyone would object to them making a new thread for their question.&nbsp; The only way thread proliferation on forums can be avoided is through merging or deletion by the moderators.&nbsp; Even if the community has strictly enforced rules on the behavior of long-time members, it's functionally impossible to force everyone who joins to know and understand these rules before clicking \"I Agree\" (you'd have to make them do like a test or captcha of the forum rules to prove that they actually read these, and at that point you're making joining the forum so difficult that few people would bother anymore, which is a lot worse for the community than just tolerating a few duplicate threads).</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:17:30.219Z",
